Practical No. 15
Securing REST API with HTTP Basic Authentication (Spring Security)
Spring Boot 3 + Maven + H2 Database + Spring Data JPA
Objective
To add Spring Security to a Spring Boot REST application, configure an in-memory user with a
BCrypt-encoded password, and secure selected endpoints so that only authenticated requests (HTTP
Basic) can access them. Notes are stored in an H2 in-memory database via Spring Data JPA.
